thread:
leah: Quick sync Meraki Bank POC: they need streaming + function calls, signed envelopes from their HSM, and a short FAQ for pricing. Any quick blockers?

ryan: JS/Go/Python SDKs support chunked streaming. Blockers: HSM-signed envelope acceptance (we support as `x-signed-envelope`) and sticky routing for cache correctness.

sec-engineer: Supported algos: ECDSA-P256, RSA-PSS. For Private we can integrate over PKCS#11. Hosted BYOK supports tenant HSM import; we don't export private keys.

ops: Pricing note: token billing unchanged. Dedicated reserved pools add a per-connection-minute for very long-lived sockets; Hosted includes connection overhead in request pricing. Send them a one-line matrix.

leah: Can we paste a tiny WS handshake example and a minimal function-call JSON they can hand to their SRE?

ryan: Handshake (JS):

```
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://edge.redwood.ai/v1/streams?model=tinygen');
ws.onopen = () => {
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({type:'auth', token: 'SHORT'}));
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({type:'start', chunked:true}));
};
```

Minimal tool call: `{"type":"tool_call","tool":"pay","input":{"to":"acct_X","amount":42.5},"idempotency_key":"uuid","schema_version":"1.0"}`

sec-engineer: Recommend idempotency ACKs: `{"type":"tool_ack","id":"...","status":"queued"}` to avoid double-exec on reconnect.

leah: Great. I'll draft the email with handshake snippet, HSM paragraph, tool schema example, and the short pricing line. Assigning runbook task.

presales-bot: Task created: meraki-poc-edge-hsm (assignees: leah, ryan) due in 2 days :white_check_mark:

ryan: FYI older Go SDK v0.9.3 had reconnect ordering quirk; recommend >=0.9.6.

